messages:
anya: heads-up: onboarding-js sampleapp gets bursts of 429s + duplicate pages when customers set prefetch=5 and client starts 20 concurrent streams. looks like connection-pool exhaustion + naive prefetch bursts are triggering server-side rate limits and then retry replays cause duplicates.

mike: can you share a tiny log snippet? is this auth-related or pure rate-limit/backpressure?

anya: logs from a local stress run:
```
INFO start stream stream=shard-12 prefetch=5
DBG open 8 connections -> pool=8/8
DBG send 5 prefetch requests -> concurrently
WARN got 429 rate_limit -> Retry-After=2s req_id=R7
DBG client retry replay old body -> fetch same cursor again
INFO stream advanced -> cursor=cur+2
DBG replayed request completes -> duplicate page
```

sofia: interesting. two issues: 1) client sends large bursts because prefetch kicks off multiple requests in parallel, 2) HTTP pool hits limit and server starts returning 429s; retries then replay stale cursors.

mike: short-term mitigation in sampleapp: add a per-stream token-bucket limiter and reduce prefetch or increase pool size. long-term: SDK should expose backpressure primitives: maxInflightPerStream, tokenBucket(rate, burst), and a retryGuard hooking into paginator state to veto replays when cursor moved.

anya: i prototyped a tiny JS limiter that helped in my run:
```
function tokenBucket(ratePerSec, burst) {
  let tokens = burst, last = Date.now();
  return async function take(n=1){
    while (true) {
      const now = Date.now();
      tokens = Math.min(burst, tokens + (now-last)/1000*ratePerSec);
      last = now;
      if (tokens >= n) { tokens -= n; return; }
      await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, 50));
    }
  }
}
// usage: await bucket.take(); fetchPage(...)
```
that reduced pool churn and 429s.

sofia: nice. SDK pattern: provide default `autoBackpressure` that coordinates prefetch with connection pool size and applies a soft limiter when pool utilization > 0.8. Also expose `maxInflightPerStream` defaulting to 2. This preserves UX while avoiding thundering bursts.

mike: we should also document recommended defaults for onboarding sampleapp: prefetch <= 2 * maxInflightPerStream and connectionPool >= prefetch. That will help customers until SDK ships autoBackpressure.

anya: another gotcha: when limiter drops a retry we should surface telemetry `paginator.replay_prevented` and a small client log so ops know replays were dropped vs server failing.

devex-bot: Created issue #7210: "sdk: autoBackpressure, maxInflightPerStream, and retryGuard to avoid burst-induced 429s and duplicate pages"

infra-bot: Staging preview for anya/prefetch-limiter available at https://staging.internal.redwood/sampleapp/branch/anya-prefetch-limiter

sofia: action items: 1) anya open PR with sampleapp token-bucket change + docs, 2) mike draft SDK API for autoBackpressure + retryGuard, 3) add e2e simulating pool exhaustion + concurrent prefetch to CI.

